  "description": "JATCAM crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C82 H86 Gd6 N18 O20 6+,3(C2 H3 N1),C1 H4 O1,6(Cl1 1-). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 5 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 5 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.569-3.872 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.37-110.85°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd6(μ3-O)(μ3-OH)4(L2)3(L3)3(L4)3(H2O)2(CH3OH)]Cl6·CH3OH·3CH3CN. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
